</script>

# Hover Card

Previews the content behind a link, such as a profile, for sighted mouse and keyboard users. Compose it from `HoverCard`, `HoverCardTrigger`, and `HoverCardContent`.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { HoverCard, HoverCardTrigger, HoverCardContent } from "#lib/components/ui/hover-card/index.js";
</script>

<HoverCard>
	<HoverCardTrigger href="https://svelte.dev">@sveltejs</HoverCardTrigger>
	<HoverCardContent>Cybernetically enhanced web apps.</HoverCardContent>
</HoverCard>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/hover-card.json
```

## Behavior

The card opens after the pointer rests on the trigger for `openDelay`, 700 milliseconds by default, or when the trigger gets keyboard focus. It stays open while the pointer is over the card, so links inside it can be clicked, and closes `closeDelay` after the pointer leaves, 300 milliseconds by default. Escape closes it. Touch screens skip it, so a tap follows the link. Use `bind:open` to read or set whether it is open, or `onOpenChange` to run code when it changes.

<Demo section="behavior" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	let open = $state(false);
</script>

<HoverCard bind:open openDelay={100} closeDelay={1000}>
	<HoverCardTrigger href="https://svelte.dev">@sveltejs</HoverCardTrigger>
	<HoverCardContent>...</HoverCardContent>
</HoverCard>
```

The card does not take focus and is not announced, so keep anything important in the page itself. Use `Popover` for content that must be reachable by every user.

## Trigger

`HoverCardTrigger` renders a link with `href` and its children. To use another element, pass a `trigger` snippet and spread its `props` onto it.

<Demo section="trigger" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<HoverCard openDelay={200}>
	<HoverCardTrigger>
		{#snippet trigger({ props })}
			<Button variant="link" {...props}>Hover me</Button>
		{/snippet}
	</HoverCardTrigger>
	<HoverCardContent>...</HoverCardContent>
</HoverCard>
```

## Side

Set `side` to `top`, `right`, `bottom`, or `left`, and `align` to `start`, `center`, or `end`. The card flips to the opposite side when there is not enough room, and shifts to stay inside the viewport.

<Demo section="side" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<HoverCard side="right" align="start">...</HoverCard>
```

## Sizes

Set `size` on `HoverCard` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg`. The default is `md`, and the padding, gap, text size, and corner radius follow the size. The card is 16rem wide; set `style="width: ..."` on the content to change it.

<Demo section="sizes" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<HoverCard size="sm">...</HoverCard>
```

## Rounded

Set `rounded` on `HoverCard` to `xs` through `4xl` or `pill` to override the radius that follows `size`. `pill` is a true pill and can clip tall content, so use `3xl` or `4xl` for round corners that stay safe.

<Demo section="rounded" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<HoverCard rounded="lg">...</HoverCard>
```

## Overrides

`HoverCardContent` takes `size` and `rounded`, which win over the hover card's for the card only.

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<HoverCardContent size="lg" rounded="lg">...</HoverCardContent>
```

## API

`HoverCard` renders no element of its own. `HoverCardContent` extends the native `div` attributes.

```ts title="index.ts"
type Props = CompPropsWithChildSimple<{
	/** Whether the card is shown; supports `bind:open` */
	open?: boolean;
	/** Called when the card opens or closes */
	onOpenChange?: (open: boolean) => void;
	/** Milliseconds the pointer rests on the trigger before the card opens; defaults to `700` */
	openDelay?: number;
	/** Milliseconds the card stays open after the pointer leaves, so it can reach the card; defaults to `300` */
	closeDelay?: number;
	/** Preferred side; flips to the opposite side when there is not enough room; defaults to `bottom` */
	side?: "top" | "right" | "bottom" | "left";
	/** Alignment along the trigger's edge; defaults to `center` */
	align?: "start" | "center" | "end";
	/** Gap in pixels between the trigger and the card; defaults to `4` */
	sideOffset?: number;
	/** Padding and text size on the shared scale; defaults to `md` */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Corner radius of the card; follows `size` when omitted. `pill` is a true pill that can clip the content, so use `3xl` or `4xl` to stay round */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}>;

interface TriggerProps {
	/** Link text for the default trigger */
	children?: Snippet;
	/** Destination of the default link trigger */
	href?: string;
	/** Custom trigger; spread `props` onto the element that opens the card */
	trigger?: Snippet<[{ props: TriggerAttrs }]>;
}

interface ContentProps extends CompPropsWithChild<"div"> {
	/** Padding and text of this card; overrides the hover card's `size` */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Corner radius of this card; overrides the hover card's `rounded`. `pill` is a true pill that can clip the content, so use `3xl` or `4xl` to stay round */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}
```
